# Who's that Pokémon?
// A Pokémon hides in its shadow:  pick its name from four, and it steps into the light.
// Only the first 151, from the very first games:  their names are the ones most kids know.

a "guess" is a thing
	its "hiding" is a pokemon
	"choices" is a new list of pokemon
	its "guessed" is a pokemon

	its "found out" is its guessed is not nothing
	its "right" is its guessed is its hiding
	its "look" is
		// In the shadow, until you've guessed
		if its found out
			return "shadow found"
		return "shadow"

	to play again
		// Four from the first 151, and one of them hides
		set first ones to first 151 pokemon of (every pokemon)
		set its choices to 4 random pokemon in first ones
		set its hiding to a random pokemon in its choices
		set its guessed to nothing

	to draw it
		if its hiding
			<segment class={its look} align="center">
				<image class="art" align="center" src={its hiding's picture} alt="A Pokémon, hiding" />
			</segment>
			draw its answer
		otherwise
			<segment class="shadow" align="center">
				<header size="huge">Who's that Pokémon?</header>
				<button color="yellow" size="massive" appearance="pill raised" onClick={play again}>Let's play!</button>
			</segment>

	to draw its answer
		if its found out
			if its right
				<header class="said" size="huge" align="center" font="title-caps">Yes!  It's {its hiding's name}!</header>
			otherwise
				<header class="said" size="huge" align="center" font="title-caps">It's {its hiding's name}!</header>
			<stack direction="horizontal" justify="center">
				<button color="yellow" size="massive" appearance="pill raised" onClick={play again}>Play again</button>
			</stack>
		otherwise
			<stack direction="horizontal" wrap justify="center">
				{draw its choice buttons}
			</stack>

	to draw its choice buttons
		for choice in its choices
			<button color="yellow" size="huge" appearance="pill raised" font="title-caps" onClick={set its guessed to choice}>{choice's name}</button>
